- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nThe given sequence is a geometric sequence with the common ratio \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$\n\nSince $|r|>1$, the sequence diverges." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-72455b3b-6d1f-5a67-aafa-1578d4066c5c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-72455b3b-6d1f-5a67-aafa-1578d4066c5c" :answer-field/id #uuid "72455b3b-6d1f-5a67-aafa-1578d4066c5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-56604a0d-b418-5a1f-a69c-467d7353d398" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3c1a4603-3748-5278-bda6-4ee7a2715131" "answer-5d2e431f-4a17-5026-87c7-8d1a7b874ade" "answer-7132648d-f2f5-51d1-9a80-097ec950b98c" "answer-70f48b0f-73e1-5598-be28-4ea95a0412d2" "answer-56604a0d-b418-5a1f-a69c-467d7353d398"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3c1a4603-3748-5278-bda6-4ee7a2715131" :answer/id #uuid "3c1a4603-3748-5278-bda6-4ee7a2715131" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Converges to $0$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5d2e431f-4a17-5026-87c7-8d1a7b874ade" :answer/id #uuid "5d2e431f-4a17-5026-87c7-8d1a7b874ade" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Converges to $0.007$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7132648d-f2f5-51d1-9a80-097ec950b98c" :answer/id #uuid "7132648d-f2f5-51d1-9a80-097ec950b98c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Converges to $\\frac{2}{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-70f48b0f-73e1-5598-be28-4ea95a0412d2" :answer/id #uuid "70f48b0f-73e1-5598-be28-4ea95a0412d2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Converges to $\\frac{3}{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56604a0d-b418-5a1f-a69c-467d7353d398" :answer/id #uuid "56604a0d-b418-5a1f-a69c-467d7353d398" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The sequence diverges" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097357 :question/problem "Consider the following sequence: \n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=-3,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$\n\nDetermine whether the sequence is convergent or divergent. If it converges, find the limit." :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $|r|=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nThe given sequence is a geometric sequence with the common ratio \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}=1.\n$$\n\nSince $r=1$, the sequence converges to ${a}_{1}=-3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096066 :answer-field/correct 17592186096069 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-6fc6aa47-4c64-51fa-b318-3ae3f17b8883" :question/id #uuid "6fc6aa47-4c64-51fa-b318-3ae3f17b8883" :question/math-academy-id "q-123338" :question/problem "Consider the following sequence: \n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{1}{4}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=2,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$\n\nDetermine whether the sequence is convergent or divergent. If it converges, find the limit." :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nThe given sequence is a geometric sequence with the common ratio \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}=-\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nSince $|r|<1$, the sequence converges to $0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-34b585ba-0fd6-572b-8c6b-6fd101f4ec8b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-34b585ba-0fd6-572b-8c6b-6fd101f4ec8b" :answer-field/id #uuid "34b585ba-0fd6-572b-8c6b-6fd101f4ec8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-070a3e55-b73d-5028-afef-baa76ead329f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4939afa2-aa64-50f4-9cba-1c80993c3641" "answer-7d409d09-a0a2-5af4-a2e1-a0549ca199ce" "answer-070a3e55-b73d-5028-afef-baa76ead329f" "answer-fee9e19e-8a29-5ea0-bb37-baf0dfd06704" "answer-530139a6-b857-5a38-aedf-d49d0b86e8a4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4939afa2-aa64-50f4-9cba-1c80993c3641" :answer/id #uuid "4939afa2-aa64-50f4-9cba-1c80993c3641" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Converges to $-2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7d409d09-a0a2-5af4-a2e1-a0549ca199ce" :answer/id #uuid "7d409d09-a0a2-5af4-a2e1-a0549ca199ce" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Converges to $-\\frac{1}{4}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-070a3e55-b73d-5028-afef-baa76ead329f" :answer/id #uuid "070a3e55-b73d-5028-afef-baa76ead329f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Converges to $0$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fee9e19e-8a29-5ea0-bb37-baf0dfd06704" :answer/id #uuid "fee9e19e-8a29-5ea0-bb37-baf0dfd06704" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Converges to $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-530139a6-b857-5a38-aedf-d49d0b86e8a4" :answer/id #uuid "530139a6-b857-5a38-aedf-d49d0b86e8a4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The sequence diverges" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f1a23838-d1bb-516b-9ae9-359aec1587f6" :question/id #uuid "f1a23838-d1bb-516b-9ae9-359aec1587f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-123336" :question/problem "Consider the following geometric sequence:\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{1}{3}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=-\\frac{3}{4},\\,n\\ge 1\n$$\n\nDetermine whether the sequence is convergent or divergent. If it converges, find the limit." :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nThe given sequence is a geometric sequence with the common ratio \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}=-\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nSince $|r|=\\frac{1}{3}<1$, the sequence converges to $0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-805dcb69-9779-5164-a339-8471bc094e31"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-805dcb69-9779-5164-a339-8471bc094e31" :answer-field/id #uuid "805dcb69-9779-5164-a339-8471bc094e31" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-64dd538a-2481-525a-b75e-3e09d1f69d00" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2cc1cf93-167d-5783-bcb1-79268c0ccdc2" "answer-407d1168-eacc-588f-9049-58098b4d1e7e" "answer-64dd538a-2481-525a-b75e-3e09d1f69d00" "answer-b89b895e-b917-5f3f-a449-e19f5273ce65" "answer-82eb318a-b526-5c90-b554-5a099c0a65ad"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2cc1cf93-167d-5783-bcb1-79268c0ccdc2" :answer/id #uuid "2cc1cf93-167d-5783-bcb1-79268c0ccdc2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Converges to $-\\frac{1}{4}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-407d1168-eacc-588f-9049-58098b4d1e7e" :answer/id #uuid "407d1168-eacc-588f-9049-58098b4d1e7e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Converges to $-\\frac{3}{4}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-64dd538a-2481-525a-b75e-3e09d1f69d00" :answer/id #uuid "64dd538a-2481-525a-b75e-3e09d1f69d00" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Converges to $0$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b89b895e-b917-5f3f-a449-e19f5273ce65" :answer/id #uuid "b89b895e-b917-5f3f-a449-e19f5273ce65" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Converges to $\\frac{1}{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82eb318a-b526-5c90-b554-5a099c0a65ad" :answer/id #uuid "82eb318a-b526-5c90-b554-5a099c0a65ad" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The sequence diverges" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097801 :tutorial/content "Suppose that the sequence $a_n$ is defined as\n\n$$\na_n =  3\\left(\\dfrac 1 2\\right)^n, \\qquad n\\geq 1.\n$$\n\nThis is a geometric sequence with common ratio $r = \\dfrac12.$ What is the behavior of this sequence as $n\\to\\infty?$\n\nLet's start by calculating the first few terms of the sequence:\n\n$$\na_1 = \\dfrac32, \\qquad a_2 = \\dfrac34, \\qquad a_3 = \\dfrac38, \\qquad a_4 = \\dfrac{3}{16}, \\qquad \\ldots\\,.\n$$\n\nPlotting the few terms of the sequence, we get a graph like the one below:\n\n![](images/8b/8b31b82126b56226a74aac5f3406d2d4ad5c85ec5c468e089acd028eba6c0469.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, it appears that $a_n\\to 0$ as $n\\to\\infty.$ This is indeed true.\n\nBecause $a_n$ approaches zero as $n\\to \\infty,$ we say that the sequence is **convergent** and that it **converges to **$0.$ We also say that the **limit of the sequence** is $0.$\n\nThe sequence is convergent because $|r| < 1,$ which causes the terms of the sequence to decrease to zero as $n$ increases." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097879 :tutorial/content "Now let's look at the sequence $b_n,$ defined as\n\n$$\nb_n =  2^n, \\qquad n\\geq 1.\n$$\n\nThis is a geometric sequence with common ratio $r = 2.$ What is the behavior of this sequence as $n\\to\\infty?$\n\nLet's start by calculating the first few terms of the sequence:\n\n$$\nb_1 = 2, \\qquad b_2 = 4, \\qquad b_3 = 8, \\qquad b_4 = 16, \\qquad \\ldots\\,.\n$$\n\nPlotting the few terms of the sequence, we get a graph like the one below:\n\n![](images/62/629ac7251857a5c79d0648e3d68d13ebfce57d560c43af1c9662636d04b5702f.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, it appears that $b_n\\to \\infty$ as $n\\to\\infty.$ This is indeed true.\n\nBecause $b_n$ grows without bound as $n\\to \\infty,$ we say that the sequence is **divergent.** The sequence is divergent because $|r| > 1,$ which causes the terms of the sequence to increase as $n$ increases." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097900 :tutorial/content "Okay, so we've seen that a geometric sequence is convergent for $|r| < 1$ and divergent when $|r| >1.$ But what about when $|r| = 1?$\n\nWe have two cases:\n\n- When $r=1,$ the geometric sequence is convergent and converges to the first term. \n\nFor example, consider the sequence $c_n = 2(1)^n,$ shown below:\n\n![](images/6f/6f11903fd259e75a51de9877fadbb97e975b48bce229bad954aae2d6b3da36c9.png)\n\nIn this case, the sequence is convergent, and the limit of the sequence is $c_1 = 2.$\n\n- When $r=-1,$ the geometric sequence is divergent. \n\nFor example, consider the sequence $d_n = 2(-1)^n,$ shown below:\n\n![](images/3e/3e4de425d4e6af816380b275e536685f524adfb33643715b093d6def3762f03a.png)\n\nIn this case, the sequence oscillates between $2$ and $-2.$ It does not approach a fixed number, so it is divergent." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097880 :tutorial/content "To summarize, suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term $a_1$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r| <    1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r| > 1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $a_1$\n\n- if $r = -1,$ the sequence is divergent" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096877 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
